# Dev Start

<!-- prism:dev-start-contract:v1 -->

Prepare, preview, and, after explicit confirmation, write one feature-only
transition:

`ready-for-dev` + `dev` -> `in-dev` + `dev`

## Usage

`$dev-start [F-XXX]`

Resolve `[F-XXX]` to exactly one existing feature file and accept only the exact
source pair above. Read SCHEMA, LIFECYCLE, status board, the complete feature, every declared
app-requirement page, any applicable API contract, linked design/context,
and workspace identity.

Use the optional read-only probe when available:

```text
prism wiki transition-preflight F-XXX [path] --action dev-start --json
```

Require envelope schema 1, command facts, capability version 2 with an
action-specific `dev-start` surface, transition version 1, target owner `dev`,
and a consistent snapshot. A version string alone is insufficient. Use direct
file checks when the probe is missing or unsupported. The preflight is copy-only
and never authorizes a write.

Check that required design/advisory prerequisites are met and inspect active
`revalidation`. An active `specification` or `design` domain blocks this
downstream start until the owning handoff verifies it. Other active delivery
domains identify work for the developer and may remain while implementation
starts. Report actual app/API evidence; a present file does not prove
implementation or shipment. Show the exact source, destination, evidence, and
feature/status board/log write set. Reread immediately before confirmation and once
after it. On confirmation, update the feature to `in-dev` with `owner: dev`,
update the status board row, and append the log entry.

Decline or cancel means no writes. If a multi-file write is partial, report each
observed change and stop for fresh recovery; no transaction is implied. This
action starts implementation and does not mark any app shipped.
